# Never let git rewrite line endings.
#
# Every file in this repo is consumed by Nix, bash, meson or patch(1) on
# Linux/macOS runners, all of which choke on CRLF:
#   * a .nix file with CRLF makes the Nix lexer emit a trailing \r inside
#     the indented string, and the phase script then dies with
#       /nix/store/...-stdenv/setup: line NNNN: $'\r': command not found
#   * a .patch file with CRLF no longer applies
#   * cross-files/*.ini with CRLF break meson's configparser
#
# "text" is deliberately unset (-text): files are stored AND checked out
# byte-for-byte, so what you see on disk is what the runner gets, on every
# platform, regardless of the user's core.autocrlf setting.
* -text
